      "message": "fix(post): doosan-dnm index writes A only for a stated A rotary\n\nThe non-RTCP indexing path formatted \"A\" itself, bypassing #1092's\nangleWord/missingLetter: a machine with clamp codes and no A rotary\nposted A words. It now refuses a turning letter the machine does not\nstate by name, refuses a turning C (this path writes only A, and used\nto drop C silently), and writes A through angleWord - byte-identical on\na machine that states A.\n\nPinned by doosan_dnm_index_names_only_a_stated_rotary.\n\nFixes #1155\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
